  "title": "Original-ball paths in Teichm\u00fcller space: an elementary corollary of Lenzhen\u2013Rafi",
  "description": "<p>An explicitly expository original-ball path corollary of Lenzhen\u2013Rafi's established uniform quasiconvexity theorem. For each fixed closed oriented surface of genus at least two, every pair of points in any original closed half-log Teichm\u00fcller ball has a continuous rectifiable path inside that same ball with length at most its ambient distance plus 4c_g. One finite topology-dependent c_g works for all centers, radii and pairs. Radial endpoint retreat followed by a minimizing segment gives the deduction and an affirmative derivation of Farb's Question 3.5 from prior geometry.</p><p>All substantive Teichm\u00fcller estimates are credited to Lenzhen\u2013Rafi. Historical priority for the elementary lemma and exact corollary is unestablished; no new substantive theorem, worldwide firstness, current openness, numerical or genus-uniform constant, or optimal Teichm\u00fcller bound is claimed. Kerckhoff's formula and Fortier Bourque\u2013Rafi's metric and nonconvexity interfaces are credited. Petyt\u2013Zalloum's 2024/2026 dual wall-space almost convexity uses a different metric, with no comparison of numerical constants. A bounded priority audit does not certify absence of prior work.</p><p>The deposit includes the full proof, TeX source, scope supplement, byte-preserved theoretical original and authored independent adversarial mathematical and source audits. No original executable was submitted; these are written verification materials, not a computational or proof-assistant certificate. Third-party paper bodies are omitted. AI tools were used extensively in deriving, verifying, adversarial review, source auditing and preparation. This is an unrefereed expository preprint; conventional human peer review and journal acceptance are not claimed.</p>",
